def "reldef:radu:annotates" "annotates — the source annotation item (thesis/argument/definition/…) reads the target source passage; a reading of the document, not a property of it (Radu Annotation model, faithful source fidelity)."
set.add name="rels" id="reldef:radu:annotates"
def "reldef:radu:connected_to" "connected to — the source annotation item is connected to the target item as Radu drew it; an intentionally NEUTRAL relation whose semantic type stays unresolved unless Radu explicitly supplied it (never inferred to supports/contradicts/defines/causes)."
set.add name="rels" id="reldef:radu:connected_to"
def "reldef:radu:in_interpretation" "in interpretation — the source annotation item belongs to the target Radu interpretation (the annotation is one annotator's reading; the same source may carry other interpretations)."
set.add name="rels" id="reldef:radu:in_interpretation"
def "reldef:radu:in_module" "in module — the source annotation item is grouped into the target module (Radu organizes elements into modules; the module boundary may itself be unresolved)."
set.add name="rels" id="reldef:radu:in_module"
def "reldef:radu:in_source" "in source — the source annotation passage belongs to the target source document (Radu Annotation model, source ≠ annotation)."
set.add name="rels" id="reldef:radu:in_source"
def "reldef:radu:orbits" "orbits — the source thesis/argument/definition orbits the target central concept (Radu's dark-blue oval the annotation elements orbit; preserved with that role and nothing more)."
set.add name="rels" id="reldef:radu:orbits"
